+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+The app wants to show how old a task is and what changed recently, but tasks carry no time information.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Every `Task` gets `createdAt` and `updatedAt`, ISO-8601 date-time strings.
+- When a task is added, both are the same time.
+- Completing, reopening, renaming, tagging or untagging a task sets its `updatedAt` to the time of the change; `createdAt` never changes.
+- The domain does not read the clock: the list is given a clock by its caller. `createTodoList` in `src/index.ts` accepts an optional clock and defaults to the real time.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `task-timestamps`: when each task was created and last changed.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/domain/task.ts`: `Task` type, `createTask` and the change functions take the time.
+- `src/domain/list.ts`: `createTaskList` takes a clock.
+- `src/index.ts`: `createTodoList` takes an optional clock. The public API changes: `Task` has two new fields and `createTodoList` has a new optional parameter (backwards compatible).
+- `test/list.test.ts`: existing whole-task assertions include the new fields.
+- Project rules touched: "No wall clock or randomness in the domain" — the domain only receives times from the caller; the only `new Date()` is in `src/index.ts`, outside `src/domain/`. "TSDoc on every exported function" and "Data is immutable" are kept (new `readonly` fields, new `@param` docs). No new dependency; no new failure paths, so no Result changes.
